[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/441940363","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/4181#issuecomment-441940363","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/4181","id":441940363,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ0MTk0MDM2Mw==","user":{"login":"sqlalchemy-bot","id":36047385,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDQ3Mzg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36047385?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2018-02-06T17:11:43Z","updated_at":"2018-11-27T06:17:33Z","body":"**Michael Bayer ([@zzzeek](https://github.com/zzzeek)) wrote:**\n\nthe events from the initial engine are propagated over to the new engine when execution_options() is called.   But there's only one event, here is your MCVE:\n\n\n```\nfrom sqlalchemy import create_engine, event\n\n\ne = create_engine(\"sqlite://\")\n\n@event.listens_for(e, \"before_cursor_execute\")\ndef _evt(*arg, **kw):\n    print \"BCE!\"\n\ne2 = e.execution_options(foo=\"bar\")\n\n\nwith e2.connect() as conn:\n    conn.scalar(\"select 1\") \n```\n\noutput:\n\n\n```\n[classic@photon2 sqlalchemy]$ python test.py \nBCE!\n[classic@photon2 sqlalchemy]$ \n\n```\n\njust one!  now.  Here is how you get *two*, and probably what your debug toolbar is doing; attach the listener to the second engine also, which it should not be doing:\n\n```\nfrom sqlalchemy import create_engine, event\n\n\ne = create_engine(\"sqlite://\")\n\n@event.listens_for(e, \"before_cursor_execute\")\ndef _evt(*arg, **kw):\n    print \"BCE!\"\n\ne2 = e.execution_options(foo=\"bar\")\n\n\n@event.listens_for(e2, \"before_cursor_execute\")\ndef _evt(*arg, **kw):\n    print \"BCE NUMBER TWO!\"\n\n\nwith e2.connect() as conn:\n    conn.scalar(\"select 1\")\n```\n\nnow you predictably get:\n\n\n```\n[classic@photon2 sqlalchemy]$ python test.py \nBCE NUMBER TWO!\nBCE!\n[classic@photon2 sqlalchemy]$ \n\n```\n\nthis is all what is to be expected.\n","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/441940363/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"sqlalchemy-bot","id":36047385,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDQ3Mzg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36047385?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://ap