s_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2018-02-06T20:47:17Z","updated_at":"2018-11-27T06:17:33Z","body":"**Antti Haapala wrote:**\n\nFirst of all, sorry, here's a proper MCVE. The target is the `Engine` class itself\n\n```\nfrom sqlalchemy import create_engine, event\nfrom sqlalchemy.engine import Engine\n\n@event.listens_for(Engine, \"before_cursor_execute\")\ndef _evt(*arg, **kw):\n    print(\"BCE!\")\n\ne = create_engine(\"sqlite://\")\ne2 = e.execution_options(foo=\"bar\")\nwith e2.connect() as conn:\n    conn.scalar(\"select 1\") \n```\n\nSo the idea there is naturally is to hook into every single `Engine`s cursor creation without prior knowledge of what engines would exist. Most notably a listener bound to `Engine` cannot even distinguish the ones fired by `Engine` and from the ones fired by `OptionEngine`. Or perhaps the target itself is incorrect?\n","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/441940365/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"sqlalchemy-bot","id":36047385,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDQ3Mzg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36047385?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subs